                <pb facs="0768" n="682" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg682"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Clayton to Mr. Algara.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic">November 18,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: Your excellency having expressed
                    a desire to see the judicial opinion upon which the Department of State bases
                    its views as to the retroactive effect of the existing treaty of extradition
                    between the two countries, I have the honor to transmit herewith a copy of the
                    same.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Powell Clayton.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
